VeridianOS: unique spacer names in externalModule.ui

The form has two spacers named "horizontalSpacer" and two named
"verticalSpacer"; uic renames the second of each and warns ("The name
'horizontalSpacer' (QSpacerItem) is already in use, defaulting to
'horizontalSpacer1'"). They now have unique names (the next free Qt
Designer suffixes). Nothing refers to them by name.

--- a/app/externalModule.ui
+++ b/app/externalModule.ui
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
-      <spacer name="horizontalSpacer">
+      <spacer name="horizontalSpacer_4">
        <property name="orientation">
         <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
        </property>
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@
     </layout>
    </item>
    <item>
-    <spacer name="verticalSpacer">
+    <spacer name="verticalSpacer_2">
      <property name="orientation">
       <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
      </property>
